1
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:09,809
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:14,990
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:21,890
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:39,079
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,080
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,080
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,080
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:43,780
(Episode 11)

9
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:46,219
Joo Yi Jae. Yi Jae.

10
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:47,819
The person at fault should take responsibility.

11
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:50,820
Why are you taking the blame? Why are you quitting?

12
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:52,120
Then who will take responsibility?

13
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,530
Between me, CEO Ahn, and Oh Ha Na, none of us did anything wrong.

14
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,830
Let's just focus on the movie, Yi Jae.

15
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:03,770
We're almost there.

16
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:06,140
Just think of it as my name being removed.

17
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,610
Nothing else will change.

18
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:08,870
What do you mean nothing will change?

19
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,210
You won't be there.

20
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:11,780
You said we'd see this through to the end.

21
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,850
I'm doing this so we can see it to the end, Yi Jae.

22
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:15,950
Please.

23
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,750
Even if this is the end for me,

24
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:21,390
the movie can't end here.

25
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:26,420
No.

26
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:28,360
I refuse to accept this.

27
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:31,300
When that incident occurred and I was losing my mind,

28
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,160
I got through it by only thinking about you.

29
00:01:33,670 --> 00:01:36,430
That you would come back. And that everything would be okay.

30
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,040
But you won't be on set? No way!

31
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:40,610
Yi Jae.

32
00:01:41,470 --> 00:01:43,370
You said you'd do everything you possibly could, right?

33
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:45,910
Now it's my turn.

34
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:29,150
Look. My ad...

35
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:30,820
has been taken down.

36
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,990
(Advertising Inquiries)

37
00:02:35,090 --> 00:02:36,430
Why are you just standing there?

38
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,030
You could at least offer me a shoulder.

39
00:02:47,510 --> 00:02:48,910
You didn't throw that photo away.

40
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:54,980
As if you ever could.

41
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,350
Well, I also make promises I can't keep.

42
00:03:09,530 --> 00:03:11,430
I know I'm paying the price,

43
00:03:14,970 --> 00:03:16,500
but can't you forgive me, just for a moment?

44
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,100
Why should I?

45
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:21,710
Because I don't want to be a coward anymore.

46
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:10,990
And do you remember "Yi Jae Will Be There"?

47
00:04:11,590 --> 00:04:13,760
I'm a woman who's been all over the country.

48
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:15,160
Just trust me.

49
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,770
Comrades, are you ready?

50
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:54,900
- Yes! - Yes!

51
00:04:56,270 --> 00:04:57,540
But where's the Assistant Director?

52
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,480
You weren't leaving without me, were you?

53
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:07,650
Seriously.

54
00:05:07,710 --> 00:05:08,950
Come on, hurry up.

55
00:05:09,010 --> 00:05:10,920
- Okay. - Hey.

56
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,579
- Gosh. - Hey.

57
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:14,690
So, shall we go save our Director Woo?

58
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:16,820
- Sounds good. - Let's go.

59
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,830
(Request and Approval for Director's Dismissal)

60
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:30,200
(For Gyeongseong Love Song, I agree to fire Director Woo Su Bin...)

61
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:31,300
(and confirm this approval in writing.)

62
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,920
(Top Line Entertainment, CEO Ahn Soo Hee)

63
00:05:49,150 --> 00:05:50,220
CEO Ahn.

64
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,360
This isn't like you. What are you doing?

65
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,460
Is that supposed to be a compliment?

66
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,400
What? Do I seem different to you?

67
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,600
No, it's just...

68
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:04,200
What is there to think about?

69
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:06,740
You can't walk away from this, CEO Ahn.

70
00:06:08,510 --> 00:06:09,510
What if I do?

71
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:11,880
Gosh, if you wash your hands of this,

72
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:15,550
who's going to cover the investment gap?

73
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:17,380
Are you telling us to clean up the mess?

74
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:20,920
In the end, this movie will just get passed around...

75
00:06:20,990 --> 00:06:23,250
and end up getting buried without a release.

76
00:06:23,790 --> 00:06:26,920
Right now, we have to make the best choice.

77
00:06:28,330 --> 00:06:29,460
And that "best choice"...

78
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,200
is to erase Director Woo's existence?

79
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:35,400
Yes, you have to. From the movie, of course,

80
00:06:35,630 --> 00:06:38,340
but also from you and Oh Ha Na.

81
00:06:39,170 --> 00:06:42,540
The moment the name Ian Woo gets attached to you two,

82
00:06:42,810 --> 00:06:46,710
the public will automatically think of this controversy.

83
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:48,680
Gosh.

84
00:06:49,150 --> 00:06:50,210
Gosh, my head hurts.

85
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:52,720
(CEO Ahn Soo Hee)

86
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:56,150
Right. It's not like I need to worry about him.

87
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,800
CEO Ahn!

88
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,330
CEO Ahn, wait a moment.

89
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:12,470
What is it?

90
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:16,870
- Who let you in? - I pushed my way in.

91
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:21,580
CEO Ahn. We can't shoot without Director Woo.

92
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:24,380
- We won't. - We'll stick with Director Woo.

93
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:26,220
This isn't some old-school movie set.

94
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:28,920
Does this kind of team still exist?

95
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:32,360
Everyone, what will you do if you get fired for this?

96
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,690
If we can't see this through together,

97
00:07:36,030 --> 00:07:37,260
then it's all meaningless.

98
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,200
CEO Ahn.

99
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,570
Our movie...

100
00:07:41,370 --> 00:07:44,540
is something we poured our hearts and souls into making.

101
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:47,970
Please keep this team intact.

102
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:53,980
So are you saying I should step down instead of Director Woo?

103
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,980
Director Woo said...

104
00:07:56,650 --> 00:07:58,380
that since this is no one's fault,

105
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,380
no one needs to take responsibility.

106
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:04,590
And yet, Director Woo stepped down on his own.

107
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:06,660
For the sake of the film.

108
00:08:09,230 --> 00:08:10,230
I also...

109
00:08:10,630 --> 00:08:12,030
want to have a happy ending...

110
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:15,330
with the person I love.

111
00:08:17,570 --> 00:08:20,540
CEO Ahn. Surely you're not going to be swayed...

112
00:08:20,610 --> 00:08:22,270
by this kind of emotional appeal.

113
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:25,910
- You have to think about losses. - What did you say?

114
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:31,080
I'm glad you said that.

115
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,720
Do you have any idea how many staff members...

116
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:34,850
- we've already lost? - Oh, please.

117
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,020
What, did you lose ten people?

118
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:40,890
We're talking about millions of dollars here.

119
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:43,030
You're still crunching numbers at a time like this?

120
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:46,530
A movie's value isn't decided...

121
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:50,400
- by your numbers game! - Film industry is a money game.

122
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,400
What's there to say about value?

123
00:08:52,470 --> 00:08:53,470
Dreams.

124
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:56,670
What?

125
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,540
A movie holds our dreams.

126
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:04,580
Right. And passion.

127
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,820
And sentiment.

128
00:09:09,290 --> 00:09:10,490
And loyalty.

129
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:13,390
Can't you see that just by looking at us?

130
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:16,530
Give me a break.

131
00:09:23,670 --> 00:09:24,670
CEO Ahn.

132
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:27,510
As for why Director Woo needs to be here,

133
00:09:28,010 --> 00:09:29,710
I think we've given you plenty of reasons.

134
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:31,880
The heart of the set...

135
00:09:33,210 --> 00:09:36,250
is the crew who are here, not the investors.

136
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:42,750
So please, make the right decision.

137
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:44,790
I'm asking you.

138
00:09:57,940 --> 00:09:58,940
CEO Ahn.

139
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:00,640
I'll think about it.

140
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:02,340
Thank you!

141
00:10:03,210 --> 00:10:04,440
- Thank you. - Thank you.

142
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:07,480
You can't, CEO Ahn.

143
00:10:07,550 --> 00:10:10,950
- You need to approve it by today. - I said I need more time.

144
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,750
What are you all still doing here? Everyone, please leave.

145
00:10:39,810 --> 00:10:44,280
(CEO Ahn Soo Hee)

146
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:46,020
(Request and Approval for Director's Dismissal)

147
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:49,090
(Current Director: Woo Su Bin)

148
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:02,530
This is my second time visiting, and I came empty-handed again.

149
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:04,900
I always think of things like this after I sit down.

150
00:11:06,300 --> 00:11:07,470
I wasn't expecting anything.

151
00:11:09,510 --> 00:11:10,810
Listen to your tone.

152
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,950
You'll just have to understand.

153
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:20,320
The only way I know how to be generous is with money.

154
00:11:21,090 --> 00:11:22,990
- Why are you here? - I just told you...

155
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:24,820
that the only way I know how to give is with money.

156
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:30,030
Go back to the set. I'll step aside.

157
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:34,169
- What? - Hey, Joo Yi Jae and the staff...

158
00:11:34,170 --> 00:11:36,500
came to see me today. And they gave me an ultimatum.

159
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:37,970
They said they won't film without you.

160
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:41,710
All that trouble just to protect one director.

161
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:44,810
Such reckless, shortsighted people.

162
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:49,650
So I've decided to just step aside.

163
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:53,680
Do you really think...

164
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:56,320
it makes any sense?

165
00:11:56,490 --> 00:11:57,920
Why wouldn't it?

166
00:11:58,690 --> 00:12:00,620
Looking at that mess, it became perfectly clear.

167
00:12:01,130 --> 00:12:03,530
That if I just step aside, this project will sail smoothly.

168
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:06,030
That it will have a happy ending.

169
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:08,500
For Ha Na...

170
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:11,240
and for you.

171
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,470
And don't worry about the investors.

172
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:17,540
Those guys will welcome it with open arms.

173
00:12:17,980 --> 00:12:19,980
I'll keep all the contracts I secured in place,

174
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:21,880
and I'll just be giving up my position.

175
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:30,860
But you'll be taking a pretty big loss.

176
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,190
What I've gained is greater.

177
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:40,900
So...

178
00:12:41,830 --> 00:12:45,170
I'm being really generous here, so just make sure you do a good job.

179
00:12:47,170 --> 00:12:48,170
Thank you,

180
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:50,940
CEO Ahn.

181
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:01,750
Well...

182
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:04,720
Su Bin.

183
00:13:08,890 --> 00:13:10,160
The happy ending that you envision.

184
00:13:13,430 --> 00:13:15,470
I truly hope you achieve it.

185
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:18,600
I will.

186
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,240
Woo Su Bin!

187
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:05,450
Shall we go?

188
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:09,820
(Jaejae Noodles)

189
00:14:10,090 --> 00:14:11,120
Look how happy they are.

190
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:28,110
It's extra good today.

191
00:14:29,270 --> 00:14:30,270
I mean...

192
00:14:30,710 --> 00:14:32,340
I was just being polite.

193
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,750
Since it's been a while since I saw the staff.

194
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:37,449
What are you talking about?

195
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:40,750
I said the gimbap is delicious.

196
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:43,790
It's delicious?

197
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:45,720
Well, you look good too.

198
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:47,320
So dazzling!

199
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:50,030
Why is your skin glowing like that?

200
00:14:50,230 --> 00:14:52,300
Should I tell the lighting director to take the day off?

201
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,600
Thank you.

202
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
What's this?

203
00:14:56,230 --> 00:14:58,040
I was just teasing you. Why are you being so serious?

204
00:14:58,640 --> 00:14:59,640
It's not that.

205
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,670
I'm thanking you for letting me start filming again.

206
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:03,510
I love you.

207
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:07,980
Of all places, you choose a gimbap shop to say that?

208
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:10,310
So you'll think of me whenever you eat gimbap.

209
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,650
And not Geum Seong Moo.

210
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,250
Are you still jealous?

211
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:18,560
- You're kind of cute. - You're cuter, Joo Yi Jae.

212
00:15:18,690 --> 00:15:19,690
Excuse me.

213
00:15:20,890 --> 00:15:22,260
How long have you been standing there?

214
00:15:22,730 --> 00:15:24,600
I'm sorry. Was that too much to listen to?

215
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:25,660
No, not at all.

216
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:27,670
Your order of 100 gimbap rolls is ready.

217
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:28,800
Enjoy.

218
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:35,269
- Hello. - Hello.

219
00:15:35,270 --> 00:15:37,410
(Gyeongseong Love Song in Production)

220
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:38,980
Director Woo.

221
00:15:42,510 --> 00:15:45,050
(Dating on set is allowed.)

222
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:47,050
- Hello. - Hello.

223
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:49,520
- Hello. - Director, it's been a while.

224
00:15:49,590 --> 00:15:52,360
- Hello. - Hello.

225
00:15:52,420 --> 00:15:55,060
- Hello. - Hello, Director.

226
00:15:55,130 --> 00:15:56,890
- You're here. - Hello.

227
00:15:57,490 --> 00:16:00,330
- Directors. - Hello.

228
00:16:00,830 --> 00:16:04,130
Director Woo, it's been so long.

229
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,500
- Goodness. - Director!

230
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:10,440
I'm trying to mark Nan Yeong's landing spot,

231
00:16:10,610 --> 00:16:11,610
and I need you to set the position.

232
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:12,780
Which scene?

233
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:14,610
We already shot it with the stunt double,

234
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:17,250
so we just need a close-up. A similar spot should work.

235
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:19,680
Right? But the martial arts director...

236
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:23,320
just keeps telling me to get your confirmation on it.

237
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:26,990
You two seem close now.

238
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,729
We're basically comrades. Right, Director?

239
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:32,400
Of course. Have you eaten? I brought some gimbap.

240
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:33,860
Hey, I bought that.

241
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,930
Everyone, Director Woo brought gimbap.

242
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,400
Grab some gimbap and eat up.

243
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:40,840
Director Woo.

244
00:16:42,170 --> 00:16:43,970
- It's been a while... - Gimbap!

245
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:46,610
- I guess I'm the gimbap? - Can I have three rolls?

246
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,850
I brought plenty. Help yourself.

247
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:52,580
The gimbap can talk. Welcome!

248
00:16:52,820 --> 00:16:54,990
- Eat up, everyone. - The gimbap is here.

249
00:16:59,290 --> 00:17:00,490
Go on, eat up.

250
00:17:23,010 --> 00:17:24,010
Cut.

251
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:33,390
- Okay! - Okay!

252
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:42,830
And that's a wrap on Gyeongseong Love Song!

253
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,330
Great work, everyone!

254
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,370
- Great work. - Great work.

255
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,370
- Great work. - Great work.

256
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:53,510
You did great.

257
00:18:37,690 --> 00:18:39,760
The Assistant Director was drinking hard again today.

258
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:43,160
See? I told you to sneakily throw out the alcohol.

259
00:18:43,230 --> 00:18:45,360
Come on, it's a happy day.

260
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,300
This won't do.

261
00:18:49,030 --> 00:18:50,030
Hop on.

262
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:51,900
Really?

263
00:18:58,340 --> 00:18:59,710
You didn't even refuse.

264
00:19:00,910 --> 00:19:04,450
This is nice. This wide back of yours.

265
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:05,720
I missed it.

266
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:09,390
- Has it been 15 years? - I don't think so.

267
00:19:09,450 --> 00:19:11,760
- What? - When you were drunk...

268
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:14,190
and slept at the hotel.

269
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:16,860
- You gave me a piggyback then too? - Yes.

270
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:19,130
How embarrassing.

271
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:22,570
You told me to use you to get ahead,

272
00:19:23,230 --> 00:19:25,340
but you gave me your back instead, Woo Su Bin.

273
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,510
- Woo Su Bin. - Yes?

274
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:33,110
You said everyone gets nervous on the first day of a shoot.

275
00:19:33,710 --> 00:19:35,810
Then what about after the last day?

276
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:37,950
Is it always this scary?

277
00:19:38,750 --> 00:19:40,720
Why? Are you scared?

278
00:19:41,690 --> 00:19:44,590
Gyeongseong Love Song already had a script,

279
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:47,930
and you were there too, so it ended like this.

280
00:19:48,830 --> 00:19:50,730
But I'm wondering if there'll be a next time for me.

281
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:54,300
And if that next time can be just as great.

282
00:19:55,470 --> 00:19:57,370
Why would you think that?

283
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:01,540
We only have better days ahead of us.

284
00:20:03,170 --> 00:20:06,140
Will you work with me next time too? And the time after that?

285
00:20:06,210 --> 00:20:07,210
Of course.

286
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:10,480
- Why of course? - Is there a reason why not?

287
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,720
You've been doing fine on your own.

288
00:20:12,820 --> 00:20:15,790
You've won many awards and received a lot of recognition.

289
00:20:16,190 --> 00:20:18,490
- You don't have to work with me... - You know why.

290
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,790
You're the reason I got into filmmaking.

291
00:20:24,730 --> 00:20:25,760
We're here.

292
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,800
- We're here already. - Yes.

293
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:37,710
Yi Jae.

294
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:40,610
It took us a long time to get here.

295
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:44,350
From now on, we can just...

296
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:47,020
walk hand in hand like this.

297
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:53,660
Okay, I understand.

298
00:20:54,630 --> 00:20:56,190
Thanks for getting me home.

299
00:20:56,830 --> 00:20:58,860
- Get home safe. - Okay.

300
00:20:59,230 --> 00:21:00,230
I'll get going.

301
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,430
Should I call you before you go to sleep?

302
00:21:04,870 --> 00:21:06,340
I'm a little tired.

303
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:08,740
Okay.

304
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:10,740
Sleep well.

305
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,540
Sweet dreams...

306
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:14,910
No, dream of me.

307
00:21:15,150 --> 00:21:16,210
Okay.

308
00:21:16,710 --> 00:21:17,710
I'm off, then?

309
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,490
Bye.

310
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:50,280
On second thought, don't dream at all tonight.

311
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:52,080
Just get a good night's sleep.

312
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,480
Okay?

313
00:21:55,750 --> 00:21:56,750
Sleep well.

314
00:21:57,820 --> 00:21:58,820
See you tomorrow.

315
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:01,690
I'm really going now.

316
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:25,850
Back then, I really wasn't afraid of anything.

317
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:42,100
(First Short Film, Woo Su Bin)

318
00:22:42,170 --> 00:22:43,530
("The Classroom of the Lost Dreamers")

319
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:45,040
("What Do I Dream Of, and for Whom Do I Die")

320
00:22:45,140 --> 00:22:47,370
("A Single Flower on a Cliff")

321
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,710
("School of Zombies")

322
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:55,310
Yi Jae, are you in here? Oh, my, you reek of alcohol.

323
00:22:55,810 --> 00:22:58,010
Gosh, what is all this?

324
00:22:58,420 --> 00:22:59,880
What a complete mess.

325
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:03,450
Gosh, she should've cleaned up while drinking these.

326
00:23:04,190 --> 00:23:05,190
Get up.

327
00:23:06,390 --> 00:23:07,790
My goodness, what is all this?

328
00:23:10,630 --> 00:23:12,630
Goodness, what in the world is that?

329
00:23:29,050 --> 00:23:30,650
Gosh, my head is killing me.

330
00:23:35,550 --> 00:23:36,820
Get up, young lady.

331
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:42,030
- Aren't you getting up? Get up now. - Gosh, that hurts!

332
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:43,590
- Get up, I said. - Stop it!

333
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:50,370
You only drank the broth. I'll get you more.

334
00:23:53,900 --> 00:23:57,010
- This is so hard. - Did someone force you to drink?

335
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:58,480
You did it to yourself.

336
00:23:58,780 --> 00:24:00,480
I'm having a hard time emotionally.

337
00:24:00,580 --> 00:24:01,580
Why?

338
00:24:02,810 --> 00:24:03,810
Mom.

339
00:24:04,580 --> 00:24:06,550
Yesterday, I rewatched the movies I made in high school...

340
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:07,620
for the first time in ages.

341
00:24:08,050 --> 00:24:10,190
And you know what? I was so embarrassed the whole time.

342
00:24:10,620 --> 00:24:14,120
Why did I film it like that? I was so full of myself.

343
00:24:14,590 --> 00:24:16,690
I suppose I was brave because I didn't know anything.

344
00:24:18,130 --> 00:24:19,530
But you know what?

345
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:21,330
Now,

346
00:24:21,430 --> 00:24:22,970
I guess I finally know a thing or two.

347
00:24:23,970 --> 00:24:27,170
- And I guess that's why I'm scared. - Goodness. You were so clueless...

348
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:29,870
running around with a camera. It's funny to think about it.

349
00:24:33,610 --> 00:24:34,610
Mom.

350
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:38,450
If I stop now with what little I know,

351
00:24:38,650 --> 00:24:40,020
I'll be neither here nor there, right?

352
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:42,950
I'll just be known as the person who got lucky with one movie, right?

353
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:44,860
I raised you wrong.

354
00:24:45,060 --> 00:24:46,760
Why are you even thinking about stopping?

355
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:50,360
Did I raise you to have these habits?

356
00:24:50,660 --> 00:24:51,660
Because when you tried to do anything,

357
00:24:51,660 --> 00:24:52,660
I always told you not to.

358
00:24:52,661 --> 00:24:55,300
- Is that why you're like this? - No, Mom, that's not it...

359
00:24:55,330 --> 00:24:57,230
If that's not it, then what do you want to do?

360
00:24:57,330 --> 00:25:00,140
Don't beat around the bush. Just tell me straight.

361
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:09,250
I don't want to stop now. I want to learn more.

362
00:25:09,550 --> 00:25:11,250
I know perfectly well that I have shortcomings,

363
00:25:11,310 --> 00:25:12,720
and I can't just stand by and pretend I don't.

364
00:25:14,020 --> 00:25:16,390
Well, there you have it. Go learn more.

365
00:25:17,450 --> 00:25:20,990
Whether it's because of me or Yeong Jae, or that Su Bin,

366
00:25:21,060 --> 00:25:23,130
don't you think about stopping for anyone.

367
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:25,630
You just follow your heart.

368
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:29,400
Mom.

369
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:33,640
Well, I should at least fry an egg.

370
00:26:38,840 --> 00:26:40,200
I haven't found her yet.

371
00:26:41,340 --> 00:26:42,440
I'm sorry.

372
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:47,740
Where could she possibly go?

373
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,850
If she's not at her parents' house,

374
00:26:49,950 --> 00:26:51,750
doesn't that mean she must be somewhere in this neighbourhood?

375
00:26:51,820 --> 00:26:53,920
She hasn't contacted Su Bin either, so...

376
00:26:54,820 --> 00:26:55,890
Director.

377
00:26:56,320 --> 00:26:58,390
Maybe it would be best to file a missing person report...

378
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:05,560
What?

379
00:27:06,100 --> 00:27:07,100
I'm sorry.

380
00:27:07,260 --> 00:27:09,030
Inside and outside the hospital,

381
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:12,440
I've already been made a complete fool of.

382
00:27:13,140 --> 00:27:14,140
And now what?

383
00:27:14,870 --> 00:27:17,040
You want me to file a missing person report on top of all this?

384
00:27:17,570 --> 00:27:20,880
What are you trying to do, announce it to the whole town?

385
00:27:44,970 --> 00:27:46,440
Of course!

386
00:27:46,870 --> 00:27:48,440
I knew it!

387
00:27:49,870 --> 00:27:52,540
Where else would you go?

388
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:54,010
You had to come back.

389
00:27:54,380 --> 00:27:57,050
You had no choice but to come back.

390
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:01,650
Let's get a divorce.

391
00:28:05,820 --> 00:28:07,820
- What? - I said, let's get a divorce.

392
00:28:15,570 --> 00:28:17,500
Divorce papers.

393
00:28:18,670 --> 00:28:19,970
Why don't we...

394
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:22,740
have a nice, quiet lunch since it's been a while?

395
00:28:23,310 --> 00:28:24,610
- Driver Kim. - Yes.

396
00:28:24,640 --> 00:28:25,880
Make a restaurant reservation.

397
00:28:25,940 --> 00:28:30,050
- Right away. - Why bother getting a license?

398
00:28:30,210 --> 00:28:33,180
What reason could you possibly have to drive?

399
00:28:33,580 --> 00:28:35,650
To get away from you.

400
00:28:36,350 --> 00:28:39,590
Who's been putting these foolish ideas in your head?

401
00:28:40,790 --> 00:28:44,560
Hwa Yeon, how can you live without me?

402
00:28:47,460 --> 00:28:50,270
You're the one who can't live without me.

403
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:54,000
It's so obvious, even after I was gone for just a short while.

404
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:58,140
- What? - I'm the one...

405
00:28:58,440 --> 00:29:03,110
who made you seem human, Woo Cheol Gyu.

406
00:29:03,710 --> 00:29:04,780
From now on,

407
00:29:04,850 --> 00:29:07,150
you can live like your true self, without me.

408
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:11,450
Because I'm going to live like my true self without you.

409
00:29:16,030 --> 00:29:17,730
All right. I guess...

410
00:29:17,790 --> 00:29:20,930
we'll have to eat at home from now on.

411
00:29:21,460 --> 00:29:22,570
Come here.

412
00:29:22,970 --> 00:29:24,030
Come here.

413
00:29:24,900 --> 00:29:26,040
Come here!

414
00:29:26,540 --> 00:29:28,000
You little...

415
00:29:36,910 --> 00:29:37,910
Have you...

416
00:29:39,180 --> 00:29:40,450
completely lost your mind?

417
00:29:40,520 --> 00:29:43,490
I'm not going to just take it anymore.

418
00:29:43,990 --> 00:29:48,060
If you don't let me go, I will tell the whole world...

419
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:50,230
what a vile person you really are.

420
00:29:50,690 --> 00:29:52,800
I have more than enough evidence.

421
00:29:54,260 --> 00:29:55,470
So,

422
00:29:55,700 --> 00:29:57,130
it's in your best interest...

423
00:29:57,200 --> 00:29:59,300
to settle the divorce as quickly as possible.

424
00:29:59,770 --> 00:30:01,040
After all, your reputation...

425
00:30:02,210 --> 00:30:04,440
is more important to you than your own life, right?

426
00:30:31,730 --> 00:30:34,799
Okay, so for the first rough cut, we've agreed to get it by next week.

427
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:36,910
Let's reschedule the meeting with the music director.

428
00:30:37,410 --> 00:30:39,210
Have you listened to all the demos they sent?

429
00:30:41,140 --> 00:30:42,550
Oh, well,

430
00:30:42,750 --> 00:30:44,250
I liked the main theme.

431
00:30:44,310 --> 00:30:46,120
It really suits Nan Yeong and Mu Gyeom.

432
00:30:49,450 --> 00:30:50,590
What's on your mind?

433
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:53,290
You seem to be having trouble focusing today.

434
00:30:54,190 --> 00:30:56,790
Sorry. When was the meeting with the music director again?

435
00:30:59,800 --> 00:31:01,500
Where did I lose you?

436
00:31:06,440 --> 00:31:07,740
I guess I've been pushing you too hard...

437
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:08,810
since filming wrapped, right?

438
00:31:09,970 --> 00:31:12,640
It's nothing urgent, so once the meeting is scheduled,

439
00:31:12,710 --> 00:31:14,210
we can talk about it again then.

440
00:31:15,010 --> 00:31:16,210
Why don't you get some rest today?

441
00:31:18,410 --> 00:31:19,450
Woo Su Bin.

442
00:31:22,050 --> 00:31:23,220
Listen...

443
00:31:23,350 --> 00:31:24,350
Yes?

444
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:25,920
Well...

445
00:31:44,170 --> 00:31:45,170
Hello?

446
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,280
Mom?

447
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:55,020
Son!

448
00:31:56,390 --> 00:31:58,150
I'm getting a divorce!

449
00:32:01,990 --> 00:32:04,890
I just threw the divorce papers at your father.

450
00:32:06,500 --> 00:32:07,960
I did the right thing, didn't I?

451
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:20,310
You've been through so much, Mom.

452
00:32:21,010 --> 00:32:22,450
You absolutely did the right thing.

453
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:26,850
Can I...

454
00:32:28,420 --> 00:32:30,490
still be...

455
00:32:31,250 --> 00:32:32,590
your mom?

456
00:32:34,220 --> 00:32:37,030
Mom. How can you even say that?

457
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:39,430
I'll always be your son.

458
00:33:05,090 --> 00:33:07,520
(Film study abroad support program)

459
00:33:10,860 --> 00:33:11,960
You're back?

460
00:33:12,430 --> 00:33:13,430
Yes.

461
00:33:14,030 --> 00:33:15,430
Why are all the lights off?

462
00:33:16,100 --> 00:33:19,100
- Have you eaten? - Not yet.

463
00:33:19,170 --> 00:33:21,040
What have you been doing if you haven't even eaten?

464
00:33:23,010 --> 00:33:24,670
What do you want to eat? What should I make you?

465
00:33:28,380 --> 00:33:29,380
What should we eat?

466
00:33:29,950 --> 00:33:30,950
Woo Su Bin.

467
00:33:31,850 --> 00:33:32,850
Yes?

468
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:35,650
Should I study abroad?

469
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:38,419
- Why? - Well,

470
00:33:38,420 --> 00:33:41,390
I've never really properly studied film.

471
00:33:43,730 --> 00:33:45,190
I think learning on set...

472
00:33:45,260 --> 00:33:47,630
is no different than taking a class for your major.

473
00:33:47,660 --> 00:33:49,270
You might even learn faster.

474
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:53,300
Then I guess I'll have to pay tuition to be on set.

475
00:33:53,570 --> 00:33:57,040
- Should we do that from now on? - You didn't know, did you?

476
00:33:57,240 --> 00:33:59,840
That the crew members went on at length explaining things only to me.

477
00:34:00,810 --> 00:34:03,110
Situations that could end with a few words...

478
00:34:03,150 --> 00:34:05,420
always turned into several sentences with me.

479
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:07,180
I know they were just trying to be nice...

480
00:34:07,250 --> 00:34:08,250
and explain things,

481
00:34:08,480 --> 00:34:10,850
but you know how it can make you feel small?

482
00:34:11,890 --> 00:34:13,990
Is this an inferiority complex about my education?

483
00:34:15,190 --> 00:34:16,330
Are you serious?

484
00:34:20,260 --> 00:34:21,260
I can't wait longer.

485
00:34:21,930 --> 00:34:24,330
I was going to tell you after we finish editing.

486
00:34:24,500 --> 00:34:25,640
Just wait here a second.

487
00:34:36,880 --> 00:34:40,180
This is our next movie.

488
00:34:43,450 --> 00:34:45,620
I wrote it when I was in the States,

489
00:34:45,890 --> 00:34:47,960
and I think you'll recognise the story when you read it.

490
00:34:49,330 --> 00:34:52,160
What? Did you write about us?

491
00:34:52,860 --> 00:34:55,800
- Yes. - That's a little...

492
00:34:55,930 --> 00:34:57,230
It's a story about completing...

493
00:34:57,300 --> 00:34:58,800
an unfinished first love through a film.

494
00:34:59,200 --> 00:35:00,500
It's perfectly cinematic, don't you think?

495
00:35:01,340 --> 00:35:03,240
Let's polish this and make it.

496
00:35:03,470 --> 00:35:06,480
I'm sure it'll be much better with your touch, Yi Jae.

497
00:35:08,850 --> 00:35:10,810
("Dream", written by Woo Su Bin)

498
00:35:13,750 --> 00:35:15,320
Is there one after this?

499
00:35:16,120 --> 00:35:17,120
Why?

500
00:35:17,590 --> 00:35:18,989
Don't you like it because it's about us?

501
00:35:18,990 --> 00:35:20,390
No, it's just...

502
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:23,190
I'm wondering how much of my future is part of your plan.

503
00:35:24,890 --> 00:35:26,930
I'm not saying we have to do this one.

504
00:35:27,100 --> 00:35:28,830
If there's a story you want to tell, we can do that.

505
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:30,330
By your side?

506
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:38,110
I should go home for dinner. You get some rest.

507
00:35:50,550 --> 00:35:51,550
Yi Jae.

508
00:35:52,120 --> 00:35:53,490
I'll read it at home.

509
00:36:01,900 --> 00:36:05,170
But if I read it and it's not good, I won't cut you any slack.

510
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:07,870
I'm telling you, I won't cut you any slack.

511
00:36:09,340 --> 00:36:10,340
All right.

512
00:36:10,970 --> 00:36:11,970
I'll get going.

513
00:36:27,920 --> 00:36:30,160
("Dream")

514
00:36:36,500 --> 00:36:39,400
(Written by Woo Su Bin)

515
00:36:48,680 --> 00:36:49,749
(2026 Bunam City International Cinema Residency)

516
00:36:49,750 --> 00:36:50,910
(Open Call for Directors)

517
00:36:50,980 --> 00:36:52,250
(Application Overview)

518
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:54,320
So, it's...

519
00:36:56,850 --> 00:37:02,090
("Dream", written by Woo Su Bin)

520
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:09,300
This place is south-facing,

521
00:37:09,370 --> 00:37:11,670
so you wouldn't believe how much sunlight it gets.

522
00:37:12,700 --> 00:37:15,040
The view is fantastic. So beautiful, right?

523
00:37:22,950 --> 00:37:24,580
Oh, my.

524
00:37:24,910 --> 00:37:28,680
Your husband is very thorough and handsome.

525
00:37:28,750 --> 00:37:32,890
- Excuse me? Well... - Honey, what about...

526
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:34,219
our bed and wardrobe?

527
00:37:34,220 --> 00:37:35,830
Don't you think that room is a bit small?

528
00:37:36,190 --> 00:37:37,230
What?

529
00:37:38,490 --> 00:37:42,670
- Landlords prefer newlyweds. - Landlords?

530
00:37:43,600 --> 00:37:46,170
If I buy this place, won't I be the landlord?

531
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:47,640
What?

532
00:37:47,700 --> 00:37:49,110
Oh, my goodness.

533
00:37:49,170 --> 00:37:51,240
I was thinking you're such a capable young couple,

534
00:37:51,310 --> 00:37:53,810
but it turns out the wife is the successful one.

535
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:59,220
That explains how I landed such a handsome husband.

536
00:38:00,120 --> 00:38:02,790
- Well, I didn't pitch in at all. - Oh, my.

537
00:38:03,350 --> 00:38:04,450
Oh, dear.

538
00:38:09,830 --> 00:38:12,660
You're really enjoying that chicken.

539
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:15,130
Filming is over.

540
00:38:15,200 --> 00:38:16,800
You have no idea how much I've held back.

541
00:38:18,470 --> 00:38:19,900
So, speaking of which,

542
00:38:19,970 --> 00:38:22,910
since filming is over, and we kissed,

543
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:25,040
what's next for us?

544
00:38:25,840 --> 00:38:27,539
Well...

545
00:38:27,540 --> 00:38:29,149
I'm asking what we'll do.

546
00:38:29,150 --> 00:38:31,210
How long are you going to keep up this formal act?

547
00:38:32,420 --> 00:38:34,380
Here are your cheese balls.

548
00:38:35,280 --> 00:38:36,850
We didn't order these.

549
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:40,290
Aren't you two celebrities?

550
00:38:40,520 --> 00:38:42,790
I was hoping I could get an autograph.

551
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:46,800
How did you know?

552
00:38:48,030 --> 00:38:50,530
I tried to be discreet, but I guess I can't hide it.

553
00:38:50,600 --> 00:38:52,740
Hey, see? I knew it.

554
00:38:53,300 --> 00:38:55,000
Can I please get your autograph?

555
00:38:55,040 --> 00:38:56,570
You're so handsome.

556
00:38:57,510 --> 00:38:59,310
- Me? - Yes.

557
00:39:01,010 --> 00:39:05,110
- I'm not really that famous. - You're an actor, right?

558
00:39:05,610 --> 00:39:08,580
Oh, you'll be famous soon. I have no doubt.

559
00:39:10,350 --> 00:39:13,860
- What's your name? - Please write Lee Su Min.

560
00:39:14,090 --> 00:39:16,590
I'll hang this in the most visible spot in my restaurant.

561
00:39:17,460 --> 00:39:19,460
Maybe I should make him wear a helmet.

562
00:39:20,260 --> 00:39:21,360
Thank you.

563
00:39:21,630 --> 00:39:24,670
Yes. And who is this person you came with?

564
00:39:26,700 --> 00:39:28,270
She's my girlfriend.

565
00:39:29,940 --> 00:39:32,140
Oh, I see.

566
00:39:33,580 --> 00:39:36,480
I'll be rooting for you, Sim Yu Geon.

567
00:39:37,450 --> 00:39:39,080
Your girlfriend is pretty too.

568
00:39:41,580 --> 00:39:42,620
All right.

569
00:39:43,420 --> 00:39:45,820
Help me.

570
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:51,990
Honestly, this kid!

571
00:39:52,430 --> 00:39:53,560
Boss.

572
00:39:53,630 --> 00:39:56,100
I'm telling you, the fish's eyes are scary.

573
00:40:03,310 --> 00:40:05,140
There. Is that better?

574
00:40:05,840 --> 00:40:06,980
Hurry up and grab a knife.

575
00:40:07,140 --> 00:40:11,610
Boss. If you put me in the kitchen, it'll be bad for business.

576
00:40:11,950 --> 00:40:13,880
You're the taste of Simsim Seafood,

577
00:40:14,050 --> 00:40:16,850
and I'm the face of Simsim Seafood. Isn't that right?

578
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:19,290
Great taste and a feast for the eyes. Right?

579
00:40:19,390 --> 00:40:22,960
If you fell in the water, only your big mouth would float.

580
00:40:23,090 --> 00:40:24,729
Do you want to carry plates for the rest of your life?

581
00:40:24,730 --> 00:40:28,530
Yes. I plan to live like this for the rest of my life.

582
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:31,030
Wandering the fish market with you, Boss,

583
00:40:31,100 --> 00:40:34,270
and chatting with the ladies there, eating good food with my mom,

584
00:40:34,340 --> 00:40:36,040
and picking on my sister a bit.

585
00:40:36,940 --> 00:40:39,140
Isn't that what happiness is?

586
00:40:42,010 --> 00:40:43,010
Right.

587
00:40:44,210 --> 00:40:46,080
That's why I'm teaching you to help you keep living like that.

588
00:40:48,850 --> 00:40:50,920
Watch what I'm doing carefully.

589
00:40:51,390 --> 00:40:53,720
See? First, cut through the fish's spine.

590
00:40:53,960 --> 00:40:55,390
Then, take everything out from the inside,

591
00:40:55,460 --> 00:40:57,430
and cut off all the fins.

592
00:41:01,160 --> 00:41:03,169
Hold it tight and chop off the tail.

593
00:41:03,170 --> 00:41:04,200
Boss.

594
00:41:08,900 --> 00:41:10,040
Won't you...

595
00:41:11,570 --> 00:41:13,040
please just tell me?

596
00:41:13,640 --> 00:41:14,910
I saw it all.

597
00:41:16,180 --> 00:41:17,410
You haven't been eating properly lately,

598
00:41:17,480 --> 00:41:19,050
but you've been taking handfuls of pills.

599
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:22,020
Those pills...

600
00:41:23,690 --> 00:41:24,690
What are they for?

601
00:41:25,590 --> 00:41:26,590
What?

602
00:41:53,120 --> 00:41:54,320
Hey, Yeong Jae.

603
00:41:56,420 --> 00:41:58,320
(Simsim Seafood)

604
00:41:58,390 --> 00:41:59,660
Yu Geon.

605
00:42:02,220 --> 00:42:04,690
What? What's wrong?

606
00:42:06,500 --> 00:42:07,800
Boss...

607
00:42:08,500 --> 00:42:10,100
No, I mean your dad.

608
00:42:11,300 --> 00:42:12,330
No...

609
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:16,110
Your dad has cancer.

610
00:42:18,640 --> 00:42:20,640
It's pancreatic cancer.

611
00:42:37,490 --> 00:42:40,100
Joo Yeong Jae, I'll be there right now.

612
00:42:42,970 --> 00:42:44,630
I said, I'm on my way.

613
00:42:47,040 --> 00:42:48,040
Sim Yu Geon.

614
00:42:49,270 --> 00:42:50,270
Thank you.

615
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:52,640
Where are you going?

616
00:42:52,940 --> 00:42:53,940
I'm sorry.

617
00:42:54,040 --> 00:42:55,640
I will come see you again some other time.

618
00:42:56,650 --> 00:42:58,650
You can't drive in your state.

619
00:43:00,820 --> 00:43:02,020
Driver Park.

620
00:43:02,690 --> 00:43:04,890
- Please give him a ride. - Yes, ma'am.

621
00:43:16,930 --> 00:43:18,700
Why didn't you tell me?

622
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:25,140
What's the point of hiding it until the very end?

623
00:43:25,570 --> 00:43:28,880
Once you're gone, what am I supposed to do?

624
00:43:29,180 --> 00:43:30,810
You just had to make me out to be a terrible son...

625
00:43:30,880 --> 00:43:32,350
to be satisfied?

626
00:43:32,980 --> 00:43:34,820
How does that make you a terrible son?

627
00:43:35,250 --> 00:43:37,519
- I was thinking of you... - If you were,

628
00:43:37,520 --> 00:43:39,050
you should've told me.

629
00:43:40,190 --> 00:43:42,390
I'm your only family.

630
00:43:43,960 --> 00:43:45,530
You should have told me.

631
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:47,700
Then we could have gone to the hospital,

632
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:49,930
started chemo, or gotten you admitted.

633
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:52,570
We would have figured something out.

634
00:43:52,840 --> 00:43:55,300
I didn't tell you because I knew you'd be like this.

635
00:43:55,370 --> 00:43:56,370
You finally...

636
00:44:00,340 --> 00:44:03,950
You finally landed a leading role and are about to get your big break,

637
00:44:04,010 --> 00:44:06,150
how could I get in your way?

638
00:44:06,720 --> 00:44:10,720
A terrible son? Fine. Since you brought it up,

639
00:44:10,750 --> 00:44:12,690
then you can be the terrible son and abandon me.

640
00:44:13,060 --> 00:44:14,860
That's better than being a father...

641
00:44:14,920 --> 00:44:16,560
who holds his son back until the very end.

642
00:44:18,230 --> 00:44:19,230
I...

643
00:44:20,630 --> 00:44:22,030
don't want to die like that.

644
00:44:22,930 --> 00:44:24,870
I can't die like that, you punk.

645
00:44:26,170 --> 00:44:28,640
I told you to visit so many times, but you stubbornly refused to come.

646
00:44:30,710 --> 00:44:33,110
So why come now and cause all this trouble?

647
00:44:40,980 --> 00:44:41,980
You...

648
00:44:44,890 --> 00:44:46,320
shouldn't come here anymore.

649
00:44:47,460 --> 00:44:51,290
After I'm gone, don't even come near this place.

650
00:44:52,160 --> 00:44:54,560
Live in Seoul forever. Got it?

651
00:44:56,230 --> 00:44:57,330
That's...

652
00:45:02,810 --> 00:45:04,370
my wish.

653
00:45:27,660 --> 00:45:28,900
He has three months.

654
00:45:29,770 --> 00:45:32,700
In three months, my dad might be gone.

655
00:45:37,140 --> 00:45:38,310
Does that even make sense?

656
00:45:41,610 --> 00:45:43,780
I've never even considered it.

657
00:45:45,750 --> 00:45:47,180
I have so many regrets.

658
00:45:49,690 --> 00:45:52,420
I should've just visited when my dad asked me to.

659
00:45:53,720 --> 00:45:56,860
Then I would've realised something was wrong sooner.

660
00:45:58,130 --> 00:46:01,160
All for some great thing I thought I was doing...

661
00:46:01,730 --> 00:46:03,500
I didn't even know he was sick.

662
00:46:05,030 --> 00:46:06,030
Yu Geon.

663
00:46:07,300 --> 00:46:09,270
Don't think that way, okay?

664
00:46:14,510 --> 00:46:15,510
Yi Jae.

665
00:46:16,880 --> 00:46:18,450
When does our movie come out?

666
00:46:19,210 --> 00:46:20,950
It's not within three months, is it?

667
00:46:21,620 --> 00:46:23,590
Can't we release it as soon as possible?

668
00:46:24,050 --> 00:46:25,050
Su Bin.

669
00:46:27,490 --> 00:46:28,690
Can't we?

670
00:46:29,420 --> 00:46:31,030
Before my dad passes away,

671
00:46:32,790 --> 00:46:34,030
I want to show him.

672
00:46:36,170 --> 00:46:38,630
Not as a son he has to look for in the background,

673
00:46:39,270 --> 00:46:41,570
but a son who fills up the screen.

674
00:46:41,940 --> 00:46:43,270
I want him to see that.

675
00:46:50,710 --> 00:46:51,810
I'm sorry.

676
00:46:53,320 --> 00:46:54,820
I shouldn't be doing this.

677
00:46:57,050 --> 00:46:58,550
I'm sorry, Su Bin.

678
00:47:03,960 --> 00:47:06,330
We may not be able to move up the release date,

679
00:47:07,460 --> 00:47:09,030
but he can still see the movie.

680
00:47:11,300 --> 00:47:12,500
Right, Woo Su Bin?

681
00:47:16,040 --> 00:47:18,670
It's not the final cut yet, so it might be a little rough.

682
00:47:19,580 --> 00:47:20,980
There won't be any music either.

683
00:47:22,410 --> 00:47:24,380
But you're in it,

684
00:47:25,050 --> 00:47:26,180
filling the whole screen.

685
00:47:32,190 --> 00:47:33,190
Thank you.

686
00:47:49,940 --> 00:47:52,240
"Sim Shin's son,"

687
00:47:52,310 --> 00:47:56,180
"Actor Sim Yu Geon's first leading de..."

688
00:47:56,480 --> 00:47:58,310
My, what a difficult word.

689
00:47:58,680 --> 00:48:00,880
It says "debut."

690
00:48:01,150 --> 00:48:04,020
"We'll be celebrating his debut."

691
00:48:04,420 --> 00:48:07,560
"Please join us." A round of applause.

692
00:48:08,120 --> 00:48:09,890
Grandma, you're the best.

693
00:48:10,190 --> 00:48:11,360
You're coming, right?

694
00:48:11,490 --> 00:48:12,760
Of course.

695
00:48:13,130 --> 00:48:16,129
- I heard about Mr. Sim. - That rude jerk.

696
00:48:16,130 --> 00:48:17,730
How could he die before an old woman like me?

697
00:48:18,130 --> 00:48:21,040
I'm going to give him a piece of my mind.

698
00:48:24,910 --> 00:48:27,280
Oh, the skies are cruel.

699
00:48:27,610 --> 00:48:29,750
Oh, I feel like I'm going to cry already.

700
00:48:29,980 --> 00:48:32,150
Goodness, Mr. Sim.

701
00:48:32,310 --> 00:48:34,920
Mom, you can't cry already.

702
00:48:35,120 --> 00:48:37,850
You're going to make me cry. Don't cry.

703
00:48:38,750 --> 00:48:41,189
Is Yeong Jae still not out of his room?

704
00:48:41,190 --> 00:48:43,760
Don't even ask. He's been crying nonstop.

705
00:48:43,830 --> 00:48:45,760
I guess I should buy him some fried chicken today.

706
00:48:46,560 --> 00:48:49,029
Oh, right. I should grab the camcorder while I'm here.

707
00:48:49,030 --> 00:48:50,330
Wait here for a second.

708
00:49:01,740 --> 00:49:04,550
- Have you eaten? - Yes, I've eaten.

709
00:49:07,780 --> 00:49:10,620
Now, where did I put it?

710
00:49:13,890 --> 00:49:15,490
Where is it?

711
00:49:18,930 --> 00:49:19,930
What?

712
00:49:22,560 --> 00:49:23,600
Hello?

713
00:49:23,670 --> 00:49:25,830
Hello, am I speaking with Director Joo Yi Jae?

714
00:49:25,900 --> 00:49:26,900
Yes, speaking. Who's this?

715
00:49:27,440 --> 00:49:28,700
My name is Kim Hyun Ji...

716
00:49:28,770 --> 00:49:30,440
from the Cultural Policy Team at Bunam City Hall.

717
00:49:30,640 --> 00:49:33,480
A few days ago, you left an inquiry regarding...

718
00:49:33,610 --> 00:49:36,110
- the residency program, right? - Yes.

719
00:49:36,480 --> 00:49:38,350
I looked into your inquiry,

720
00:49:38,410 --> 00:49:41,480
and you mentioned your film hasn't been released yet.

721
00:49:42,220 --> 00:49:43,220
Yes.

722
00:49:43,290 --> 00:49:46,090
In that case, you can still apply with an unfinished version...

723
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:47,490
that's currently in editing.

724
00:49:48,660 --> 00:49:50,659
However, there are some additional documents...

725
00:49:50,660 --> 00:49:53,160
you'll need to submit. Can you take these down?

726
00:49:53,230 --> 00:49:55,230
Yes, just a moment.

727
00:49:58,670 --> 00:50:01,040
Shall I begin?

728
00:50:01,370 --> 00:50:02,370
("Dream", written by Woo Su Bin)

729
00:50:02,940 --> 00:50:04,610
Yes, go ahead.

730
00:50:06,580 --> 00:50:08,510
A director's certificate.

731
00:50:09,880 --> 00:50:12,350
A consent to submit for review form. Yes.

732
00:50:13,480 --> 00:50:14,750
The production company's official seal.

733
00:50:15,520 --> 00:50:16,789
A letter of recommendation?

734
00:50:16,790 --> 00:50:17,820
Okay.

735
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:19,520
Okay, thank you.

736
00:50:20,090 --> 00:50:21,090
Okay.

737
00:50:28,560 --> 00:50:29,560
You scared me.

738
00:50:37,810 --> 00:50:38,870
(A director's certificate...)

739
00:50:39,570 --> 00:50:41,110
("Dream", written by Woo Su Bin)

740
00:50:42,110 --> 00:50:44,180
I wasn't trying to hide it.

741
00:50:45,410 --> 00:50:46,780
I haven't even applied yet.

742
00:50:48,980 --> 00:50:51,050
I guess you really didn't like my script.

743
00:50:52,620 --> 00:50:53,620
Well...

744
00:50:54,660 --> 00:50:55,860
I haven't read it yet.

745
00:50:57,090 --> 00:50:58,130
Because if I read it,

746
00:50:59,160 --> 00:51:01,100
I'd want to keep holding on to you.

747
00:51:04,900 --> 00:51:05,900
And what's wrong with that?

748
00:51:07,740 --> 00:51:08,740
Yi Jae.

749
00:51:09,540 --> 00:51:10,540
You said you were scared.

750
00:51:11,770 --> 00:51:13,410
Stay with me. It's okay.

751
00:51:15,080 --> 00:51:16,080
You're right.

752
00:51:16,650 --> 00:51:18,480
If I stay with you, I guess there's nothing to be scared of.

753
00:51:18,710 --> 00:51:19,980
I can just depend on you.

754
00:51:22,280 --> 00:51:23,290
But if I do that,

755
00:51:25,450 --> 00:51:26,460
will I be okay with myself?

756
00:51:28,190 --> 00:51:29,190
And will you be okay?

757
00:51:30,330 --> 00:51:31,990
Why wouldn't we be?

758
00:51:33,860 --> 00:51:35,760
I don't understand why you're being like this.

759
00:51:36,430 --> 00:51:37,500
You.

760
00:51:37,800 --> 00:51:39,370
I'm being like this because of you.

761
00:51:40,040 --> 00:51:42,540
I know if I stay by your side, I'll stop moving forward.

762
00:51:43,000 --> 00:51:44,640
That's why I have to leave.

763
00:51:45,940 --> 00:51:47,040
But I like you so much,

764
00:51:47,610 --> 00:51:49,140
and I don't want to break up with you.

765
00:51:49,680 --> 00:51:51,150
It's driving me crazy trying to decide.

766
00:51:51,550 --> 00:51:52,610
Why would you stop moving forward?

767
00:51:53,380 --> 00:51:54,580
I won't let you.

768
00:51:55,080 --> 00:51:56,250
That's not it. I also need to, on my own...

769
00:51:56,320 --> 00:51:57,420
Don't go.

770
00:51:58,650 --> 00:51:59,990
I don't want to be away from you.

771
00:52:03,330 --> 00:52:04,330
You...

772
00:52:05,730 --> 00:52:07,400
You're so selfish.

773
00:52:08,930 --> 00:52:12,370
I can struggle with this decision, but you can't be doing this to me.

774
00:52:13,030 --> 00:52:15,270
You were away for over ten years,

775
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:18,170
so now you're saying I can't make any choices at all?

776
00:52:20,880 --> 00:52:22,480
I'm asking you to choose me.

777
00:52:24,980 --> 00:52:26,520
You're more important to me than movies.

778
00:52:29,120 --> 00:52:31,420
My dream isn't about making movies.

779
00:52:32,120 --> 00:52:33,150
It's you, Joo Yi Jae.

780
00:52:37,230 --> 00:52:38,560
Don't go, Yi Jae.

781
00:52:39,230 --> 00:52:40,260
Okay?

782
00:53:15,630 --> 00:53:16,970
Why are you holding on to that?

783
00:53:17,300 --> 00:53:20,370
- Give it here. Let's toss it. - No, why throw it out? It's fine.

784
00:53:21,600 --> 00:53:24,040
Have you seen everything? We can go now, right?

785
00:53:25,910 --> 00:53:26,910
Yes.

786
00:53:27,940 --> 00:53:28,940
I guess so.

787
00:53:30,580 --> 00:53:31,580
Dad.

788
00:53:34,050 --> 00:53:35,580
You've worked so hard.

789
00:53:37,650 --> 00:53:39,650
It's time to put down your knives...

790
00:53:41,320 --> 00:53:42,320
and pick up your guitar.

791
00:54:01,610 --> 00:54:04,980
(You're invited to a screening of Gyeongseong Love Song.)

792
00:54:07,120 --> 00:54:09,120
For ten years, I was only on screen for an hour,

793
00:54:09,650 --> 00:54:11,220
but now, I'm in the whole two-hour movie.

794
00:54:13,490 --> 00:54:14,490
Is that so?

795
00:54:15,690 --> 00:54:16,990
I'll see for myself the day after tomorrow.

796
00:54:21,400 --> 00:54:23,130
(Sim Shin's son, Actor Sim Yu Geon's first leading debut)

797
00:54:23,200 --> 00:54:24,370
(We'll be celebrating his debut.)

798
00:54:32,570 --> 00:54:33,810
But what should I do?

799
00:54:35,510 --> 00:54:36,610
I have a date that day.

800
00:54:39,310 --> 00:54:41,920
I think you can bring your date.

801
00:54:42,420 --> 00:54:43,420
You think you can handle it?

802
00:54:48,890 --> 00:54:50,090
Actor Sim Yu Geon.

803
00:54:51,330 --> 00:54:54,130
First leading debut. Gosh, that's awesome.

804
00:54:54,230 --> 00:54:56,000
(Thanks to you all, it's never been dull.)

805
00:54:56,130 --> 00:54:57,130
You did well.

806
00:54:57,200 --> 00:54:59,500
(Simsim Seafood will take a break. From Sim Shin)

807
00:55:10,250 --> 00:55:13,110
- You worked so hard. - Oh, hello.

808
00:55:13,210 --> 00:55:14,750
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

809
00:55:14,850 --> 00:55:16,850
- Hello. - Hello.

810
00:55:31,530 --> 00:55:32,530
Yi Jae.

811
00:55:34,770 --> 00:55:35,770
You made it?

812
00:55:36,710 --> 00:55:38,369
- We're here. - We're here.

813
00:55:38,370 --> 00:55:40,840
Oh, you worked so hard. Gosh.

814
00:55:40,910 --> 00:55:43,010
- Hey, over here. - Come on, say hello.

815
00:55:43,080 --> 00:55:46,580
- Oh, my. - Hey, Su Bin.

816
00:55:48,580 --> 00:55:50,150
- Come here. - Look at Sung Chan.

817
00:55:50,220 --> 00:55:51,420
- Come here. - Come over here.

818
00:55:51,490 --> 00:55:54,390
- Come here. - You're looking prettier every day.

819
00:55:54,460 --> 00:55:56,890
- Go say hi to your uncle. - You have to say hello.

820
00:55:56,960 --> 00:55:57,960
Hello.

821
00:55:59,560 --> 00:56:02,830
- Hey. How have you been? - That's a good boy.

822
00:56:03,200 --> 00:56:04,900
- Come here, Sung Chan. - Yes, come over here.

823
00:56:04,970 --> 00:56:06,700
- Come on, over here. - Honey, watch out for a car.

824
00:56:06,770 --> 00:56:07,770
Be careful.

825
00:56:08,870 --> 00:56:10,140
Whose car is that?

826
00:56:10,670 --> 00:56:13,610
Director! I'm here too.

827
00:56:16,310 --> 00:56:18,150
Oh Ha Na! I'm a fan.

828
00:56:18,780 --> 00:56:20,620
That looks heavy. Here, let me get that for you.

829
00:56:20,920 --> 00:56:22,380
Who are you?

830
00:56:22,450 --> 00:56:23,590
- Oh, he's... - I am...

831
00:56:23,690 --> 00:56:25,990
Director Joo Yi Jae's only brother,

832
00:56:26,050 --> 00:56:28,260
Joo Yeong Jae.

833
00:56:28,320 --> 00:56:29,560
It's a pleasure to meet you.

834
00:56:30,020 --> 00:56:31,430
In that case, could you take this for me?

835
00:56:31,490 --> 00:56:32,530
Yes, of course.

836
00:56:33,530 --> 00:56:34,530
By the way, where's Yu Geon?

837
00:56:34,660 --> 00:56:37,400
- He's inside the hall. Go on in. - Okay.

838
00:56:37,570 --> 00:56:38,570
Well...

839
00:56:39,330 --> 00:56:40,940
She left without even saying hi to me.

840
00:56:41,100 --> 00:56:43,970
You must be close with her. Sim Yu Geon really made it.

841
00:56:46,040 --> 00:56:47,040
Gosh, you!

842
00:56:51,610 --> 00:56:52,650
Yu Geon.

843
00:56:54,450 --> 00:56:55,450
Ha Na.

844
00:56:57,820 --> 00:56:59,090
What are you doing here?

845
00:57:02,390 --> 00:57:04,690
I came to give you a shoulder to lean on.

846
00:57:09,530 --> 00:57:11,800
Why did you make me get all dressed up in a suit?

847
00:57:13,570 --> 00:57:14,570
What should I do?

848
00:57:15,940 --> 00:57:17,510
Hello, Father.

849
00:57:18,570 --> 00:57:19,570
Hello.

850
00:57:20,840 --> 00:57:22,480
- Yes. - Oh, right.

851
00:57:22,940 --> 00:57:25,950
Aren't you that actress who co-stars with Yu Geon?

852
00:57:26,180 --> 00:57:27,180
Yes.

853
00:57:27,880 --> 00:57:30,450
But what are you two...

854
00:57:32,620 --> 00:57:35,060
It's a pleasure to meet you.

855
00:57:35,320 --> 00:57:38,730
I'm Oh Ha Na, Yu Geon's girlfriend.

856
00:57:38,890 --> 00:57:40,090
I see.

857
00:57:43,330 --> 00:57:44,330
Excuse me?

858
00:57:45,370 --> 00:57:47,500
Yes, she's my girlfriend.

859
00:57:47,740 --> 00:57:48,740
She's...

860
00:57:49,440 --> 00:57:52,810
your girlfriend?

861
00:57:56,010 --> 00:57:58,550
Well, you really are a good son.

862
00:57:58,750 --> 00:57:59,950
A good son, indeed.

863
00:58:00,850 --> 00:58:02,080
He's a good son, right?

864
00:58:05,090 --> 00:58:07,460
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

865
00:58:07,620 --> 00:58:09,020
- It's starting. - It's starting.

866
00:58:09,160 --> 00:58:10,330
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

867
00:58:16,700 --> 00:58:18,130
That's my friend.

868
00:58:19,030 --> 00:58:22,000
That's my friend, Sim Yu Geon. You got this!

869
00:58:26,210 --> 00:58:27,210
What do you think?

870
00:58:28,040 --> 00:58:29,480
Not under the lanterns of Wolhwajeong,

871
00:58:29,810 --> 00:58:31,350
but me, bathed in this moonlight.

872
00:58:32,350 --> 00:58:33,350
I don't know.

873
00:58:33,650 --> 00:58:35,080
No matter how I look at you,

874
00:58:35,150 --> 00:58:36,750
you don't seem to have a single worry.

875
00:58:37,120 --> 00:58:40,490
No matter how I look, it's truly beautiful.

876
00:58:41,620 --> 00:58:44,490
The me that's reflected in your eyes.

877
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:50,370
Why must you turn everything into a joke?

878
00:58:52,970 --> 00:58:54,140
Each of us...

879
00:58:54,970 --> 00:58:58,370
lives our life as if we're making a film.

880
00:59:06,480 --> 00:59:08,620
Just as every film has its iconic scenes,

881
00:59:12,920 --> 00:59:14,220
every life...

882
00:59:15,690 --> 00:59:17,030
has them too.

883
00:59:18,030 --> 00:59:19,230
I haven't seen you around before.

884
00:59:19,560 --> 00:59:21,000
My name is Nan Yeong.

885
00:59:24,470 --> 00:59:25,500
I can see it.

886
00:59:39,410 --> 00:59:42,550
I couldn't even protect you. So how can I protect my country?

887
01:00:03,340 --> 01:00:05,370
(This movie is dedicated to Sim Shin, Actor Sim Yu Geon's father.)

888
01:00:10,850 --> 01:00:11,980
Iconic scenes...

889
01:00:13,510 --> 01:00:15,520
are made from countless other scenes...

890
01:00:16,250 --> 01:00:17,350
piled on top of another.

891
01:00:17,450 --> 01:00:20,890
(This movie is dedicated to Sim Shin, Actor Sim Yu Geon's father.)

892
01:00:46,150 --> 01:00:48,680
In a life that won't even make it to 60,

893
01:00:50,280 --> 01:00:52,120
I've been given a moment I'll never forget.

894
01:00:53,520 --> 01:00:54,590
Thank you.

895
01:00:57,760 --> 01:00:58,790
Today,

896
01:00:59,130 --> 01:01:02,630
seeing the dream my son has magnificently achieved,

897
01:01:02,930 --> 01:01:04,870
it reminds me of my own dreams from when I was young.

898
01:01:05,600 --> 01:01:08,000
I have no regrets as I prepare to leave this world,

899
01:01:08,240 --> 01:01:09,899
but this old father wants to leave behind...

900
01:01:09,900 --> 01:01:11,710
at least one great moment of his own.

901
01:01:12,040 --> 01:01:14,040
Would that be all right with all of you?

902
01:01:14,340 --> 01:01:17,010
- Yes. - Yes!

903
01:01:27,720 --> 01:01:28,720
Well done.

904
01:01:30,220 --> 01:01:31,230
You did great.

905
01:01:32,430 --> 01:01:33,430
Thanks.

906
01:01:51,710 --> 01:01:57,450
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

907
01:02:44,030 --> 01:02:45,630
I know for certain.

908
01:02:47,240 --> 01:02:48,440
The next scene...

909
01:02:49,270 --> 01:02:50,300
that I must write.

910
01:02:58,050 --> 01:02:59,310
Don't go, Yi Jae.

911
01:03:00,150 --> 01:03:01,150
Okay?

912
01:03:08,390 --> 01:03:09,390
Su Bin.

913
01:03:12,460 --> 01:03:13,830
I love you,

914
01:03:16,100 --> 01:03:17,300
but my dream isn't you.

915
01:03:18,830 --> 01:03:20,600
I already chose you once,

916
01:03:21,600 --> 01:03:22,640
and that choice...

917
01:03:23,670 --> 01:03:25,410
made me miserable for a long time.

918
01:03:28,680 --> 01:03:30,280
This time, I'm not getting off the bus.

919
01:03:32,550 --> 01:03:33,780
This time, instead of choosing you,

920
01:03:35,650 --> 01:03:37,050
I'm going to chase my dream.

921
01:03:53,200 --> 01:03:57,100
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

922
01:04:29,440 --> 01:04:30,440
I...

923
01:04:30,940 --> 01:04:33,740
decided to let Woo Su Bin go...

924
01:04:36,540 --> 01:04:37,950
for my own iconic scene.

925
01:05:20,920 --> 01:05:22,960
(Dream To You)

926
01:05:23,220 --> 01:05:25,130
So I'm going to stop loving you!

927
01:05:25,260 --> 01:05:27,030
Why are you making me say something like this?

928
01:05:27,400 --> 01:05:29,259
Let's use this chance to say a proper goodbye...

929
01:05:29,260 --> 01:05:30,500
and move on.

930
01:05:30,560 --> 01:05:33,030
- Choi Sa Rang? - What? Where did it all go?

931
01:05:33,230 --> 01:05:35,500
- What are you listening to? - My dad's guitar performance.

932
01:05:35,570 --> 01:05:38,010
Joo Yi Jae. Rather than holding you back,

933
01:05:38,040 --> 01:05:40,310
I hope this gives you the strength to keep going.

934
01:05:40,610 --> 01:05:42,210
This dream I rediscovered thanks to you.

935
01:05:42,340 --> 01:05:43,340
I'm going to make it...

936
01:05:43,341 --> 01:05:44,380
even bigger and better for the next two years.

937
01:05:44,450 --> 01:05:46,550
It's not too late. Go to Yi Jae.

938
01:05:47,420 --> 01:05:49,920
I guess I still haven't gotten over you.